{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2162-02-28 13:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hello, I'm Dr. Lee. I understand you've been having trouble swallowing and some pain when you eat?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2162-02-28 13:05:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, it's been going on for weeks. Food feels stuck in my throat, especially solids. And it hurts right at my trach site when I swallow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2162-02-28 13:06:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. And you mentioned liquids sometimes go down the wrong way?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2162-02-28 13:06:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, not like choking, but I feel them going into my airway. It’s scary."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2162-02-28 13:07:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Given your history of tracheobronchomalacia and tracheostomy, we need to be careful. We’ve ordered a chest X-ray to check for infection or other issues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2162-02-28 13:08:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. Could this be related to my trach or past surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2162-02-28 13:09:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly. Scar tissue or inflammation from prior reconstructions could affect swallowing. We’ll look into that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2162-02-28 15:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your chest X-ray came back. Good news — no pneumonia or lung issues. Your trach and Port-A-Cath are stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2162-02-28 15:21:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. But why am I still having trouble swallowing?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2162-02-28 15:22:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We think it might be related to swelling or reflux. You’ve had GERD before, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2162-02-28 15:23:05",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, and I’ve been feeling more heartburn lately."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2162-02-28 15:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That could be contributing. We’re going to start you on a higher dose of your reflux medication for now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2162-02-28 15:25:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will that help the pain when I swallow?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2162-02-28 15:26:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It should, over a few days. But we also want to do a swallowing study with barium to see exactly what’s happening."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2162-02-28 15:27:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that safe with my trach?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2162-02-28 15:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it’s very safe. A speech therapist will help guide it. We need to check if food or liquid is going into your airway."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2162-02-28 17:40:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just checking in. We’ve scheduled your swallowing study for tomorrow morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2162-02-28 17:41:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, thanks. I’ve been sticking to soft foods and thickened liquids. It helps a little."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2162-02-28 17:42:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. That’s smart. We’ll keep you on that until we get more answers."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2162-03-01 09:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your swallowing study was done this morning. I have the results."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2162-03-01 09:16:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "How did it go? Did you see where the problem is?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2162-03-01 09:17:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. The upper part of your throat is quite swollen, which explains the feeling of food getting stuck."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2162-03-01 09:18:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that from infection?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2162-03-01 09:19:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not likely. There’s no sign of infection. But we did see that stomach contents are coming all the way up into your throat."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2162-03-01 09:20:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, so that’s why things taste sour sometimes?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2162-03-01 09:21:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. And that acid is probably causing the swelling and pain. We also saw a small hiatal hernia, which can make reflux worse."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2162-03-01 09:22:40",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is there a fistula? I was worried food might be going into my trach."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2162-03-01 09:23:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I’m glad you asked. The study shows no tracheoesophageal fistula. That’s a relief. But we did see thin liquids penetrating into your airway, though not full aspiration."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2162-03-01 09:24:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So what does that mean for me?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2162-03-01 09:25:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It means we need to keep using thickened liquids and soft foods for now. The speech therapist will give you specific instructions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2162-03-01 09:26:40",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the reflux? Can we fix that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2162-03-01 09:27:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re already treating it with stronger medication. Over time, that should reduce the swelling and improve swallowing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2162-03-01 09:28:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I need surgery for the hernia?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2162-03-01 09:29:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not right now. We’ll manage it medically first. If symptoms persist, your gastroenterologist can discuss options later."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2162-03-01 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One more thing — your dentist noted a possible abscess on one of your teeth. Have you had tooth pain?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2162-03-01 11:01:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Now that you mention it, yes — my lower right molar has been aching."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2162-03-01 11:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It might be contributing to the discomfort when you swallow. We’ll note it for your dentist to treat after discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2162-03-01 16:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. We’re planning to discharge you this evening."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2162-03-01 16:31:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. What should I do at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2162-03-01 16:32:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Continue the reflux medication, stick to soft foods and thickened liquids, and follow up with your pulmonologist and primary care provider."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2162-03-01 16:33:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the tooth?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2162-03-01 16:34:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "See your dentist soon for the abscess. We’ll send them a note."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2162-03-01 16:35:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I feel much better knowing what’s going on."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2162-03-01 16:36:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. We’ll make sure you have all the instructions before you leave."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2162-03-01 17:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just confirming — you’re cleared to go home. Nurse will give you discharge papers."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2162-03-01 17:01:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. I’ll follow everything you said."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2162-03-01 17:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. Call us if swallowing gets worse or you develop fever or breathing issues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2162-03-01 17:03:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks again, Doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2162-03-01 17:04:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care. Get some rest."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2162-03-01 17:05:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I plan to."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2162-02-28 13:04:00",
    "admission_end": "2162-03-01 18:04:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with a history of tracheobronchomalacia, bronchopulmonary dysplasia, tracheostomy, and multiple airway reconstructions was admitted due to persistent dysphagia, odynophagia, and cough over several weeks. She reported difficulty swallowing solids, pain at the trach site, and liquids going down the wrong way. A chest X-ray showed no pneumonia. A barium swallow study revealed upper pharyngeal edema, gastroesophageal reflux reaching the pharynx, and a small hiatal hernia, but no tracheoesophageal fistula. She was managed with optimized reflux treatment, dietary modifications, and speech therapy guidance. A periapical abscess was noted and referred for dental follow-up. She improved clinically and was discharged with instructions for continued reflux management, soft diet, and outpatient follow-up.",
    "problems": [
      "Dysphagia, unspecified",
      "Chronic obstructive asthma, unspecified",
      "Esophageal reflux",
      "Depressive disorder, not elsewhere classified",
      "Periapical abscess without sinus"
    ]
  }
}
